g a little bit of that flaring  coming into play this is something that  you know smartphones are having a hard  time with you know it's just part and  parcel with the way the lens is designed  but i mean if you use it correctly it  can be quite creative now let's look at  another shot here of the main camera to  show the difference now of course this  is gonna be high resolution the colors  are much more punchier as you can see  before edit and after edit but a lot of  play in the files and look at the detail  in his his shirt  his jacket here the backpack there's a  lot of detail here which is nice because  usually portrait mode you lose detail  because of all the ai coming into play  but samsung's done a pretty good job in  terms of maintaining detail but giving  that portrait uh you know that  background defocus so you can play with  that a little bit more okay now let's  look at the main camera here in terms of  low-light photography this has been  edited a little bit you can see that i  was focusing right here there's enough  detail here noise reduction is coming  into play but it looks relatively good  this is before edit and then here is  after edit  before edit and after edit this is what  the main camera very impressive for  lower light photography here is with  night mode all right  now you're going to see a little bit  more that hdr look coming into play here  as most night modes do but it does a  relatively decent job of maintaining  detail still with some decent dynamic  range this is before edit and then after  edit before edit after edit i always  recommend just kind of punching the  colors up to your liking with any sort  of photography out there because nothing  straight out of camera will look optimal  here's a great shot that i took with the  main camera just to kind of show you the  detail that it's able to capture even a  lower light photography of this uh  dragon head here look at how sharp this  is this looks absolutely fantastic with  the buildings in the background this is  with the main camera  uh here's before edit and here's after  edit before edit and after edit  absolutely love the uh the quality  coming out of this main camera this is  samsung's best cameras to date honestly  really really impressed with it and  here is  the uh three-time zoom as well so we  show this in the video but look at the  detail when you look up close this is  absolutely awesome and if you think this  is sort of  this is so if you think this is sort of  uh you know mushy here this of course is  a painted dragon so this is actually  what you're seeing it looks like almost  like watercolors because that's what it  looked like in person but the detail  there is really really stunning a couple  more shots here of these tigers portrait  mode look at the detail that we're  seeing here  the paint structure here the detail  through  the tiger's head and through the paws  and the legs absolutely awesome really  impressed with that  [Music]  and let's talk about black and white  photography because you can do this with  the filters in the s22 ultra with any of  the cameras and it's actually very  impressive so if you do like black and  white photography you're going to really  like what this camera provides again  you're not going to get as much noise  because of course just black and white  but i mean this is really really nice  very happy with the images that i got  out of this as well  look at the detail here very very  impressive i would say the black and  white gives you a little bit more detail  than even the color on that matter but  again black and white versus color  you're always going to get that okay  let's go into macro real quick because i  was talking about macro photography  and unfortunately as i mentioned it's  not as good as the iphone okay so uh  this is  yeah not good  a couple shots here i tried to zoom in  on this it's really pixelated folks so  while  i mean i think samsung tried to add this  macro capabilities it's not as good as  what the iphone is producing right now  maybe that'll improve with a firmware  update in the near future so anyway  those are some shots from lightroom  let's go back to my final thoughts  all right as we saw from lightroom the  image quality out of the s22 ultra is  very impressive for a smartphone  especially the main camera now the wide  angle lower light not so good in  brighter conditions it actually fares  quite decent the telephoto lenses the  three times to me is the sweet spot it's  still really sharp uh really good  clarity to the image 10 times is  struggling a little bit i'm not going to  do 100 times zoom honestly speaking we  tried it but it's not it's neither here  nor there it's more of a gimmick to me  than anything else you're never going to  use it uh but let's talk about video for  a second because this is where i also  think the ls22 ultra does really shine  8k only in good light but again would  you use 8k i don't know i think 4k 1080  is going to be the sweet spot for most  people even 1080 for the you know  because of instagram tick tock you can't  do 4k and that stuff yet right and  that's primarily how people are going to  use their smartphones for creating  content is in of that range but if you  are a professional videographer and you  do want to like a sort of a small b cam  i think the 4k will definitely suffice  in that regard the colors coming out of  the the sensors are great uh the clarity  uh the image quality is just is really  really good even for photography i mean  this is the best samsung camera system  i've seen on any of their phones to date  they've really done a great job with it  but this is still early in 2022 i mean  right now this is the king of the  smartphones in my personal opinion when  it comes to image quality i think  samsung's knocked it out of the park a  lot of the great features as i mentioned  the microphone option where you can  select which microphone you want the  front to the 